The **CBSE Class 10 Mathematics syllabus for 2025-26** is organized into seven main chapters (“units”) with detailed subtopics and competencies.[1]

## Chapter Names and Subtopics

### Number Systems

- Real Numbers
  - Fundamental Theorem of Arithmetic
  - Proofs of irrationality of $$ \sqrt{2} $$, $$ \sqrt{3} $$, $$ \sqrt{5} $$
  - Properties and applications of real numbers[1]

### Algebra

- Polynomials
  - Zeros of a polynomial
  - Relationship between zeros and coefficients (for quadratic polynomials)
- Pair of Linear Equations in Two Variables
  - Graphical method of solution, consistency/inconsistency
  - Algebraic solution: substitution and elimination
- Quadratic Equations
  - Standard form
  - Solution by factorization & quadratic formula
  - Nature of roots (discriminant)
- Arithmetic Progressions
  - nth term, sum of n terms, applications in problems[1]

### Coordinate Geometry

- Concepts of coordinate geometry
- Distance formula
- Section formula (internal division)[1]

### Geometry

- Triangles
  - Similarity criteria and properties
  - Basic Proportionality Theorem (Thales’ theorem) and converse
- Circles
  - Tangent to a circle (definition, theorems)
  - Properties of tangents[1]

### Trigonometry

- Introduction to Trigonometry
  - Trigonometric ratios, values for $$ 30^\circ, 45^\circ, 60^\circ $$
  - Relationships between ratios
- Trigonometric Identities
  - Proof and application of $$ \sin^2A + \cos^2A = 1 $$
- Heights and Distances
  - Simple problems involving angles of elevation and depression ($$ 30^\circ, 45^\circ, 60^\circ $$), maximum two right triangles[1]

### Mensuration

- Areas Related to Circles
  - Areas of sectors and segments, perimeter/circumference problems
- Surface Areas and Volumes
  - Cubes, cuboids, spheres, hemispheres, right circular cylinders/cones, and combinations of two solids[1]

### Statistics and Probability

- Statistics
  - Mean, median, mode of grouped data (avoid bimodal situations)
- Probability
  - Classical definition
  - Simple problems related to everyday events[1]

## Chapter Table

| Chapter Name               | Main Subtopics [1]                                                                  |
| -------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Number Systems             | Real Numbers, Fundamental Theorem, Irrationality proofs                             |
| Algebra                    | Polynomials, Pair of Linear Equations, Quadratic Equations, Arithmetic Progressions |
| Coordinate Geometry        | Distance Formula, Section Formula                                                   |
| Geometry                   | Triangles (Similarity criteria), Circles (Tangents, Theorems)                       |
| Trigonometry               | Trig Ratios, Identities, Heights & Distances                                        |
| Mensuration                | Areas (Sectors, Segments), Surface Areas & Volumes                                  |
| Statistics and Probability | Mean, Median, Mode (Grouped Data), Probability                                      |

Every subtopic is designed to align with the prescribed NCERT textbooks and focus on both conceptual understanding and applications.[1]

